{%- comment -%}
  anatole's `partials/footer.html`, which the theme renders **twice** with different
  class modifiers — the CSS then shows exactly one of them:

    footer__sidebar → inside the sidebar column; hidden below the desktop breakpoint
    footer__base    → after the wrapper; `display: none` on desktop (mobile only)

  Emitting only one leaves the footer invisible at that breakpoint, which is what
  happened here: the site had no copyright line on desktop at all.

  `{% render %}` is scope-isolated in LiquidJS, so everything this needs is passed in
  rather than read off `site`.
{%- endcomment -%}
<footer class="footer footer__{{ modifier }}">
  <ul class="footer__list">
    <li class="footer__item">
      {%- comment -%}
        Escape before turning newlines into breaks, so a multi-line copyright keeps its
        shape without letting raw markup through.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      &copy; {{ year }} {{ copyright | default: author | markdownify }}
    </li>
  </ul>
</footer>
